#  AY001: Breath Response and Recovery Experiment

## Objective

To observe the response of the BME688 gas sensor following exposure to human breath and characterise the recovery behaviour after exposure.

## Setup

Hardware:
- ESP32 microcontroller
- BME688 gas sensor
- TFT display

The sensor was monitored under normal environmental conditions before introducing breath exposure.

## Observations

### Baseline

The sensor displayed stable environmental readings prior to breath exposure.

Baseline measurements were recorded from the TFT display.

### Breath Exposure Response

Human breath was introduced to the sensor between approximately 11.04 seconds and 14.80 seconds.

A rapid decrease in gas resistance was observed during this ~3 second exposure period, indicating a measurable sensor response.

### Recovery

Following breath exposure, the sensor gradually returned towards its baseline value.

Recovery occurred from approximately 14.80 seconds to 1 minute 15.88 seconds (~61 seconds).

## Summary

The prototype demonstrated:

- A rapid response to breath exposure
- A measurable change in gas resistance
- A gradual recovery phase towards baseline

## Next Steps

- Repeat measurements to assess consistency
- Quantify response magnitude and recovery time
- Improve breath sampling control
